 "answer": "**I’d recommend she skip the outdoor walk today, Saturday, October 17.** Singapore’s official update reported unhealthy air quality, with 1-hour PM2.5 readings in the **Elevated to High** bands; NEA advises older adults to minimize outdoor activity, and to avoid all outdoor activity for the next hour when PM2.5 is High. ([weather.gov.sg](https://www.weather.gov.sg/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026/))\n\nAn indoor walk would be a safer substitute. If she’s considering going out anyway, check the latest **1-hour PM2.5 reading for her area** in NEA’s myENV app just beforehand—the readings can change. If she has heart or lung disease, be especially cautious.([weather.gov.sg](https://www.weather.gov.sg/haze-situation-update-17-october-2026/))",
